.\" Man page for nubifer-security-scan
.\" Generated for NubiferOS
.TH NUBIFER-SECURITY-SCAN 1 "January 2026" "NubiferOS" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
nubifer-security-scan \- run security scans on NubiferOS systems
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B nubifer-security-scan
[\fIOPTIONS\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B nubifer-security-scan
is a security scanning tool for NubiferOS that checks for vulnerabilities,
audits system hardening, and verifies ISO signatures. It integrates with
the NubiferOS Security Dashboard to provide a unified view of system security.
.PP
Scan results are saved to \fI~/.local/share/nubifer/security/\fR as JSON files
and can be viewed in the Security Dashboard or processed programmatically.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-\-vuln-scan
Run a vulnerability scan on the system using grype. Scans installed packages
for known CVEs and generates a report sorted by severity.
.TP
.B \-\-compliance
Run a hardening compliance audit using lynis. Checks system configuration
against security best practices and generates a hardening score (0-100).
.TP
.BI \-\-verify-iso " ISO"
Verify the GPG signature of an ISO file. Requires the ISO file path and
expects a corresponding .asc signature file.
.TP
.B \-\-full
Run all security scans (vulnerability scan and compliance check).
Equivalent to running \fB\-\-vuln-scan\fR and \fB\-\-compliance\fR together.
.TP
.BI \-\-target " PATH"
Specify a target path for vulnerability scanning instead of the root
filesystem. Useful for scanning mounted ISOs or chroot environments.
.TP
.B \-\-json
Output results in JSON format to stdout. Useful for scripting and
integration with other tools.
.TP
.BR \-q ", " \-\-quiet
Suppress non-essential output. Only errors will be displayed.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
Success. All scans completed without critical issues.
.TP
.B 2
Critical vulnerabilities found. Review the vulnerability report.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I ~/.local/share/nubifer/security/vuln-scan.json
Vulnerability scan results in JSON format.
.TP
.I ~/.local/share/nubifer/security/compliance.json
Compliance audit results in JSON format.
.TP
.I ~/.local/share/nubifer/security/full-scan.json
Combined results from a full scan.
.TP
.I /usr/share/nubifer/nubiferos-signing-key.pub
Public GPG key for ISO signature verification.
.SH EXAMPLES
.PP
Run a vulnerability scan:
.RS
.nf
$ nubifer-security-scan --vuln-scan
.fi
.RE
.PP
Run a full security audit:
.RS
.nf
$ nubifer-security-scan --full
.fi
.RE
.PP
Get JSON output for scripting:
.RS
.nf
$ nubifer-security-scan --vuln-scan --json | jq '.by_severity'
.fi
.RE
.PP
Verify an ISO signature:
.RS
.nf
$ nubifer-security-scan --verify-iso nubiferos-1.0.iso
.fi
.RE
.PP
Scan a mounted ISO filesystem:
.RS
.nf
$ sudo mount -o loop nubiferos.iso /mnt/iso
$ nubifer-security-scan --vuln-scan --target /mnt/iso
.fi
.RE
.SH DEPENDENCIES
.TP
.B grype
Required for vulnerability scanning. Automatically installed if not present.
.TP
.B lynis
Required for compliance auditing. Automatically installed if not present.
.TP
.B gpg
Required for ISO signature verification.
.SH SECURITY CONSIDERATIONS
.PP
Vulnerability scans require network access to download the latest CVE database.
The grype database is cached locally and updated periodically.
.PP
Compliance audits may require root privileges to check certain system
configurations. Run with sudo for complete results.
.PP
Scan results may contain sensitive information about system vulnerabilities.
Protect the results directory appropriately.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR nubifer-dashboard (1),
